# Known-flaky behavior scenarios.
#
# Format: <scenario> <TAB> <reason>
# Lines starting with # are comments. When a listed scenario FAILS, the
# test-behavior recipe prints KNOWN-FLAKY + the reason and exits 0 (so
# batteries don't block on tracked issues). Re-run with strict=1 to treat a
# listed scenario's failure as a hard failure.
#
# Entries must carry a tracked issue reference and the observed failure
# signature — a flake without a reason is an unfiled bug, not a registry
# entry.
#
# Resolved entries are removed, not kept: the seed pinning + the fixes make
# flakes reproducible, so a re-added entry should cite what regressed.
#
# Seed pinning removes GEOGRAPHY variance, not TICK-TIMING variance: the
# sweep's cycle list is built via pairs() (hash order can differ per process),
# so same-seed runs can still diverge slightly in timing. Assertions must carry
# margins/retries, and position-based thresholds are timing-fragile.

upgrade-threshold	intermittent low-leg timeout (observed ~1 in 3 runs): the LOW-evolution upgrade replacement occasionally does not appear within the phase budget. Partially addressed: processPendingUpgrades' state-2 create now retries at the nearest free position when create_entity returns nil (the original was already destroyed in state 1, so a blocked position silently LOST the structure) and counts upgrade.createBlocked — check that counter in a failing run to confirm the trigger. Remaining suspects: the double-queue (rescan + onBuild both queue the same entity; the duplicate's state-1 pass drops when the entity is already invalid — believed harmless), the base-formation timing (the upgrade is queued on base formation), and pendingUpgradesLength accounting (queueCreation's >100 guard would block creations if the length leaks). (logs: /tmp/rampant-behavior-upgrade-threshold.out)

#
# Resolved (removed) entries, for the record:
#   siege-settle   - was ~50-60% seed-sensitive. Fixed by the evolution-
#                    rescan purge fix (f18c225) + the on_init expansion
#                    cooldown override. Now 3/3 pinned seeds.
#   migration-settler - was 2/6 seed-sensitive. Same purge-fix cause.
#                    Now 3/3 pinned seeds.
